# Kiirunavaara demo on Splunk Cloud

The EC2 host in eu-north-1 was terminated. That AWS plan is retired. Do not run `setup-splunk-enterprise.sh`, `demo-start.sh`, `demo-pipeline.sh`, or `create-app-bucket.sh` to build a new host.

The demo target is the existing Splunk Cloud stack where the operator has `sc_admin`. Confirm Victoria Experience under Support & Services → About. Upload `lkab_kiruna_demo` as a private app. Create the events index `kiruna_events` if the install does not. Enable the modular input on one search head only.

Do not use the AWS Deployments plugin to generate CDK, CloudFormation, Terraform, Elastic Beanstalk, ECS, or App Runner. Do not ask for AWS keys, a Splunk password, or a license file. Do not write those into the repo.

The app tree is `lkab_kiruna_demo/` on branch `cursor/kiruna-app-v0.1`. If this checkout does not contain it, stop and say so. Do not invent the app. Validation that needs Splunk Web stays a person in the browser.